      "artist": "Teemu008 from Palatine, Illinois",
      "description": "Washington Place, a national landmark in Honolulu, HI (1847). It often served as a home for American politicians. When Liliʻuokalani married John Owen Dominis in 1862, it became the private home of the princess (future queen).  Liliʻuokalani was arrested there in 1893 during the overthrow of the monarchy. She was then confined there after her release from ʻIolani Palace. She then lived in the house freely for the rest of her life. In 1918, the house became the executive mansion for the territorial and state governors of Hawaii. It ceased this role in 2002.",
